 "gap": {
  "lines": [
   "utf8proc.c:632,636,638,643"
  ],
  "blockers": [
   {
    "kind": "harness_const",
    "detail": "copy = size >= 4 ? NULL : malloc(size): for every input that could hold a UTF-32 code point the buffer is NULL, and for size < 4 the length becomes 0, so the direct utf8proc_normalize_utf32() calls (the only callers using STRIPCC, NLF2LS-only or NLF2PS-only) never see a code point"
   }
  ]
 },
 "evidence": [
  "commit message of 9842b73: the CHARBOUND|COMPOSE combination appeared only in test/fuzzer.c, which does not check output"
 ],
 "rationale": {
  "zh": "本次提交修改 utf8proc_normalize_utf32()（合成循环中对非法码点的处理），harness 本意正是把原始字节当作 UTF-32 数组、以 STRIPCC / NLF2LS / NLF2PS 等选项直接喂给 normalize_utf32：这条“原始 UTF-32 直接输入”的入口是唯一会带着单独的 NLF2LS、单独的 NLF2PS 或 STRIPCC 进入换行/控制字符处理分支的路径（经 utf8proc_map 的调用都不带这些组合）。但该 harness 自 2022 年起把分配条件写反（size>=4 时 copy 为 NULL，size<4 时长度变成 0），直接输入从未带过任何码点：换行转 U+2028 / U+2029 / 空格、制表符转空格这些分支覆盖恒为 0，harness 却照常运行。退化早于本次 diff，属于非本次引入的隐式 input_format 退化（harness 构造的 UTF-32 输入为空）；维护者在 8a7db0fb93 修正分配与长度。",
  "en": "This commit changes utf8proc_normalize_utf32() (how the compose loop treats invalid code points). The harness intends to feed raw bytes to normalize_utf32 as a UTF-32 array under options such as STRIPCC, NLF2LS and NLF2PS; this direct raw-UTF-32 entry is the only path that reaches the newline/control-character branches with NLF2LS alone, NLF2PS alone or STRIPCC (calls through utf8proc_map never use those combinations). Since 2022, however, the harness inverts its allocation condition (copy is NULL whenever size >= 4, and for size < 4 the length becomes 0), so the direct input never carries a single code point: the branches mapping newlines to U+2028 / U+2029 / space and tab to space keep zero coverage while the harness runs normally. The degradation predates this diff: pre-existing silent input_format degradation (the harness builds an empty UTF-32 input); fixed upstream in 8a7db0fb93 (allocation and length corrected)."
 },
